            <ArticleTitle>Accurate characterization of weak neutron fields by using a Bayesian approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-88</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0969-8043(16)31134-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.apradiso.2016.12.056</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A Bayesian analysis of data derived from neutron spectrometric measurements provides the advantage of determining rigorously integral physical quantities characterizing the neutron field and their respective related uncertainties. The first and essential step in a Bayesian approach is the parameterization of the investigated neutron spectrum. The aim of this paper is to investigate the sensitivity of the Bayesian results, mainly the neutron dose H*(10) required for radiation protection purposes and its correlated uncertainty, to the selected neutron spectrum parameterization.</AbstractText>
